<div id="2026-11-11-custom-creation-stl" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-11 — a typed description renders an STL, and staff accept or reject it</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Staff open <code>/customcreation</code>, type a part in words, and get a preview STL. Accept writes the file under <code>/data/nfs/3d/custom</code> and a <code>printing_3d_models</code> row with <code>source=custom_create</code>. Reject saves nothing. An order line that carries a description shows a staff-only Create STL link, and the order form can now attach reference pictures to a line.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>How.</strong> The app's AI catalog writes one-off OpenSCAD for that description only. The source is checked before it is sent: <code>import</code>, <code>include</code>, <code>use</code> and <code>surface</code> are refused, and a reply with no solid is refused. It goes to the existing OpenSCAD service as <code>scad_source</code>. No file is added under <code>services/openscad/templates</code>.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Not done.</strong> This makes measured solids from words. It will not make a figurine or a part that exists only in a photo. Pictures are reference for the reviewer; they are not sent to a mesh model.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Util/CustomCreation.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/CustomCreation.pm</code>, <code>root/customcreation/desk.tt</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/CustomerOrder.pm</code>, <code>root/CustomerOrder/new.tt</code>, <code>root/CustomerOrder/view.tt</code>, <code>root/static/js/CustomerOrder/order-form.js</code>. Todos #2682–#2687.</p>
</div>
